+# Task 001 inspection notes
+
+Selected todo:
+
+> Inspect the current `/get-started` controller/templates or LiveView, auth sign-in token creation, return-to handling, Staff request inbox, and onboarding request creation/notification code.
+
+## `/get-started` route and rendering
+
+- `/get-started` is a controller-rendered page, not a LiveView.
+- Routes live in `web/lib/memba_web/router.ex`:
+  - `GET /get-started` -> `MembaWeb.PageController.get_started/2`
+  - `POST /get-started` -> `MembaWeb.PageController.submit_get_started/2`
+- Controller/template files:
+  - `web/lib/memba_web/controllers/page_controller.ex`
+  - `web/lib/memba_web/controllers/page_html/get_started.html.heex`
+- Current behaviour:
+  - Signed-out `GET /get-started` renders one form with name, email, club name, and note.
+  - Signed-in identities are only treated specially when their email belongs to an existing Membership Person.
+  - A signed-in identity with no Person currently falls through to the signed-out form path, so the page would ask for and trust typed name/email.
+
+## Current request submission and notification path
+
+- `PageController.submit_get_started/2` calls `get_started_request_attrs/2`, then `Memba.Onboarding.create_request/2`.
+- On successful creation it immediately calls `Memba.Onboarding.NewRequestEmail.deliver/1`, then redirects to `/get-started?submitted=true`.
+- For signed-in existing-Person requesters, `get_started_request_attrs/2` ignores typed `requester_name` and `requester_email`, merges the Person name plus signed-in email, and passes `requester_person_id`.
+- For signed-out requesters, all submitted request fields are passed directly to `Onboarding.create_request/2`.
+- Staff notification is currently a web-controller side effect after request creation. `Onboarding.create_request/2` itself does not deliver notification emails.
+
+## Onboarding request storage and domain behaviour
+
+- `Memba.Onboarding.create_request/2` builds `Memba.Onboarding.Request.create_changeset/2` and inserts into the `onboarding_requests` table.
+- `Request.create_changeset/2` currently requires `requester_name`, `requester_email`, `requested_club_name`, and `note`.
+- `requester_email` is normalized through `Memba.Membership.EmailAddresses.normalize_email/1`.
+- `requester_person_id` is optional and supplied only via opts.
+- Request submission does not create Membership read-model/domain records today. Conversion is the code path that creates/reuses Person, creates Club, creates Membership, assigns Membership Admin role, marks request converted, and sends the welcome email.
+- There is currently no domain/API-level way to express “verified identity email required”; any caller can pass any `requester_email` to `Onboarding.create_request/2`.
+
+## Magic-link auth and return-to handling
+
+- Sign-in UI is `MembaWeb.AuthLive.SignIn` at `/auth` and `/auth/check-email`.
+- It calls `Accounts.request_sign_in_link/1`, then delivers through `Memba.Accounts.AuthEmail.deliver_sign_in_link/3`.
+- `Accounts.request_sign_in_link/2` only creates tokens for staff emails or known active member emails. Unknown public requester emails deliberately return `{:ok, nil}`.
+- `Accounts.create_sign_in_token/2` can create a sign-in token for any normalized valid email without membership eligibility checks.
+- Token consumption is in `MembaWeb.AuthController.callback/2` at `/auth/sign-in/:token`.
+- `AuthController.callback/2` supports return-to in either:
+  - query param `return_to`, or
+  - session key `IdentityAuth.return_to_session_key()`.
+- Because `IdentityAuth.log_in_identity/2` renews and clears the session, callback reads `return_to` before logging in. Query-param `return_to` is important for links opened without the original browser session.
+- `safe_return_to/1` accepts local paths beginning with `/` except `//`, plus safe club URLs.
+- For non-staff identities, callback redirects to `safe_return_to(return_to) || "/"`.
+- For first-time staff emails, callback still redirects to `/auth/onboard` and stores the safe return-to for staff onboarding.
+
+## Staff request inbox and triage
+
+- Staff inbox is `MembaWeb.Admin.RequestsLive.Index` at `/admin/requests`.
+- It loads `Onboarding.list_active_requests/0`, which lists rows with `status == "active"` ordered oldest-first.
+- There is no separate “verified” flag/filter in the inbox; the intended iteration slice can keep Staff-visible data verified by only creating `onboarding_requests` after verified submission.
+- Rejection uses `Onboarding.reject_request/3` and removes the row from the LiveView stream.
+- Conversion uses `Onboarding.convert_request_to_club/3`, removes the row, and may flash welcome-email delivery errors.
+
+## Tests already covering current behaviour
+
+- `web/test/memba_web/controllers/page_controller_test.exs`
+  - current signed-out full request form;
+  - current signed-in existing-Person read-only form;
+  - signed-out request creation and Staff notification;
+  - signed-in existing-Person submission ignores forged name/email.
+- `web/test/memba_web/controllers/auth_controller_test.exs`
+  - sign-in link request/neutral acknowledgement;
+  - known member/staff token creation;
+  - unknown-recipient no-token behaviour;
+  - callback consumption and stored/query return-to handling.
+- `web/test/memba/onboarding_test.exs`
+  - create/list/reject/convert request basics.
+- `web/test/memba/onboarding_conversion_test.exs`
+  - conversion creates or reuses Person, creates Club/Membership, assigns Admin, and sends welcome email.
+- `web/test/memba_web/live/admin/requests_live/index_test.exs`
+  - Staff active inbox, rejection, conversion, existing-Person reuse, and no requester rejection email.
+- `acceptance-tests/features/request_account.feature` already contains iteration-030 scenarios tagged `@todo-domain @todo-ui`.
+
+## Implementation seams for later tasks
+
+- The signed-out email-only step likely needs a Get Started-specific wrapper that:
+  - validates/normalizes the email;
+  - calls `Accounts.create_sign_in_token/2` rather than `Accounts.request_sign_in_link/2`, because public requesters may not be known members yet;
+  - delivers `AuthEmail.deliver_sign_in_link/3` with a callback URL containing `return_to=/get-started`;
+  - does not call `Onboarding.create_request/2` or `NewRequestEmail.deliver/1`.
+- The signed-in form logic needs to distinguish:
+  - existing Person: known name/email read-only; collect club name/note;
+  - no Person: verified email read-only; collect name, club name, note.
+- Verified request submission should use `current_identity.email` as the requester email and ignore/reject any typed requester email.
+- Domain-level request creation should gain an explicit verified-email input/requirement so direct callers cannot create Staff-visible requests with arbitrary unverified emails.
+
+## ADR conformance notes
+
+- No ADR is explicitly referenced by the iteration plan.
+- Relevant accepted ADRs inspected:
+  - ADR 0001: Phoenix remains the web delivery stack.
+  - ADR 0002 and ADR 0009: Membership conversion remains Commanded/event-sourced with Ecto projections, while onboarding requests are an existing Ecto source-of-truth exception.
+  - ADR 0010: shared `acceptance-tests/features/request_account.feature` remains the cross-runner behavioural source.
+  - ADR 0013: future browser-facing coverage should prefer feature-style Phoenix tests, with lower-level Conn/LiveView tests where they better expose controller/session mechanics.
+  - ADR 0021 and ADR 0022: projection synchronization matters for later acceptance/domain absence checks; this inspection did not change projector behaviour.
